menu "Simulator options"

config APP_SENSOR_COUNT
	int "Simulated CGM sensors / BLE identities"
	range 1 4
	default 4
	help
	  One physical board simulates this many independent CGM sensors, each
	  with its own BLE identity / advertising set / CGMS instance and its own
	  fully independent config slot. 1 == the original single-sensor build.
	  Keep CONFIG_BT_ID_MAX / BT_MAX_CONN / BT_EXT_ADV_MAX_ADV_SET /
	  BT_CGMS_INSTANCE_COUNT in prj.conf equal to this.

config APP_CGMS_NO_AUTH
	bool "Drop the authenticated-link requirement on CGMS characteristics"
	default y if APP_SENSOR_COUNT > 1
	default n
	help
	  Fallback for the Windows LE Secure Connections pairing failure against
	  the board's non-default BLE identities. When set, the standard CGM
	  Service characteristics use BT_GATT_PERM_READ / WRITE instead of
	  *_AUTHEN, so a client streams glucose with no pairing at all
	  (acceptable for a simulator).

	  Defaults on for multi-sensor builds (APP_SENSOR_COUNT > 1): "Option B"
	  (privacy off + static addresses + peripheral-initiated security) was
	  tested on hardware and still fails on identities 1..N-1 — the board
	  logs "Security failed ... err 2" (AUTH_REQUIREMENT) and Windows drops
	  the link. Single-sensor builds default off and keep the real security
	  model (identity 0 pairs fine).

config APP_CGMS_STAGGER_NOTIFY
	bool "Round-robin the CGMS instances' periodic notifications"
	default y if APP_SENSOR_COUNT > 1
	default n
	help
	  Normally every instance's report_meas work item fires at
	  the same instant each comm_interval (they are all initialised back to
	  back at boot), so the N measurement notifications hit the controller
	  as one burst. When set, instance k is delayed by k/N of a comm_interval
	  (N = BT_CGMS_INSTANCE_COUNT), spreading them across the interval.

	  Defaults on for multi-sensor builds. Measured on hardware 2026-10-03
	  (scripts/ble_ab_batch.py, two-minute runs, 4 sensors connected at once):
	  with this on, no sensor went silent in 12 of 12 runs; with it off,
	  Sensor 4 accepted start_notify and then never notified in 12 of 12
	  runs. Only connecting Sensor 4 first on its own avoided it.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config SETTINGS
	default y

config ZMS
	default y if (SOC_FLASH_NRF_RRAM || SOC_FLASH_NRF_MRAM)

config NVS
	default y if !(SOC_FLASH_NRF_RRAM || SOC_FLASH_NRF_MRAM)
